course: dictionary
lesson: 1953
title: Community: one word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. «In a community people do different jobs: farmers grow food, doctors treat illness, teachers teach, builders build.» The clues are jobs and people, so community means all the people who live in one place.
explain: «Community police officers visit schools to help children stay safe, not only to catch people.» Here community describes the police, so it means the people of one area, and the officers help those people. Check by swapping in your meaning: "police officers who work for the local people" still makes sense.
explain: Community can also mean a group who share something. «Interfaith friendship means people of different beliefs learning about each other and serving the community together.» Here the people share a belief and a purpose, so community means a group that comes together. In science, a community is all the living things that live together in one habitat, such as the plants, frogs and insects in a pond.
fact: Community means all the people who live in one place, such as a town or neighbourhood.
fact: A community can also be a group of people who share something, like a religion, a hobby or a language.
fact: In science, a community is all the living things that live together in one habitat.
fact: Useful phrases: local community, community centre, school community, community service.
fact: «Palmares» in Brazil was a community of escaped enslaved people, and it lasted for most of the 1600s.
exercise: «In a community people do different jobs: farmers grow food, doctors treat illness, teachers teach, builders build.» What does community mean here? | A rule that everyone must follow | A kind of pond with frogs | A type of food | *All the people who live in one place
exercise: In science, what is a community? | Only the people in a town | A group of plants in a pot | A school trip to the countryside | *All the living things that live together in one habitat
exercise: Which phrase names a building where local people can meet? | community police | school community | *community centre | community service
test: «Escaped enslaved people formed free communities called maroon settlements in Jamaica, Suriname, Brazil and elsewhere.» What does community mean in this sentence? | A group of frogs and insects | A kind of soldier | A school trip | *A group of people who live together and share their lives
test: Which meaning fits «Interfaith friendship means people of different beliefs learning about each other and serving the community together»? | All the living things in one habitat | A single family in one house | A place to buy food | *A group of people who share beliefs and come together
exam: Ella reads «Community police officers visit schools to help children stay safe.» Which meaning of community fits best? | A kind of rescue dog | A type of school lesson | *The people of one area, whom the officers serve | A group of frogs living in a pond
